{
  "package": "strings",
  "notes": "Go's strings are byte strings that may hold invalid UTF-8. For valid text the symbol is std (`str` methods, `String`, `slice::join`); `tools/strings_check.py` runs both std and `BytesExt` against Go on valid UTF-8 and checks they agree. Where std differs (empty separators, Go's simple case mapping, EqualFold, cutset-free predicates on invalid bytes) it is `rust_stdlib::text::BytesExt` on `&[u8]`, with Go's U+FFFD-of-width-1 rule. Reader and Replacer are `rust_stdlib::text`. Go index -1 is Option<usize>; runes are char.",
